<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63638" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῑτότης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῑτός</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>plainness, simplicity</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόσμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					274
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν στεφάνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					142
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν λ. διώκουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					2.59
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. διαίτης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cic.
					<u>Fam.</u>
					7.26.2
				</span></i>
			; cj. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεπτότης</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Sent.Vat.</u>
				63
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Gramm., a
			figure of speech, <i>assertion by means of understatement</i> (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μείωσις</span>) or <i>negation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Serv.
			</span></i> ad Verg.<i><span class="en">
				<u>G.</u>
				2.125
			</span></i>, Donat.ad Ter.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Hec.</u>
				775
			</span></i>.</div>
